Third-party notices for ZX Sidekick
===================================

The program is built from the Rust crates named below, for Linux, macOS and Windows, and from
SDL3, compiled into it from the source that the sdl3-src crate carries. Each licence text is given
once, with the crates under it named above it.

SDL3's licence is the zlib licence used by sdl3-src that opens with Sam Lantinga's copyright. The
other texts used by sdl3-src are the notices of parts of SDL3 by other authors, as they stand in
its source, among them HIDAPI's and yuv2rgb's licences.

Every crate is used unmodified. The source of each is at https://crates.io/crates/<name>/<version>,
except aym, rustzx-core and rustzx-z80, which come from https://github.com/zx-sidekick/rustzx
(see THIRD-PARTY.md). ZX Sidekick's own source is at https://github.com/zx-sidekick/zx-sidekick.
